<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Republican Party (United States)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1854">1854</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Grand Old Party</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Republican Party is one of the two major political parties of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, founded in 1854 by opponents of the expansion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a> into the western territories. Its first successful presidential candidate, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abraham-lincoln">Abraham Lincoln</a>, was elected in 1860, and it dominated national politics for much of the period until 1932; it is often called the Grand Old Party (GOP).</p></div>
